# Citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2.0): GitHub shows "Cite this repository"
# from this file, and Zenodo uses it for releases. Keep it in step with app/__init__.py,
# pyproject.toml and codemeta.json (tests/test_fair_metadata.py checks them).
#
# TODO(owner) before the first release:
#   - confirm the author list; add ORCIDs, affiliations and any co-authors;
#   - add `license:` (SPDX id) once LICENSE exists (README "License");
#   - add `date-released:` and the Zenodo DOI (`doi:` / `identifiers:`) when v3.0.0 is tagged.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "SPROUTS (Root-Mask-and-Skeletons)"
abstract: >-
  SPROUTS is a desktop application (PyQt6 and PyTorch) for plant-root phenotyping
  from minirhizotron images. A ResNet-18-based segmentation network predicts root
  masks and a Pix2Pix-style generator predicts root skeletons, both from the original
  images; masks and skeletons can be corrected by hand in built-in editors. Root area
  (mm²) and root length (mm) are computed from a calibrated camera field of view and
  exported as CSV files, explored in interactive Dash/Plotly dashboards, and a
  multi-class ground-truth tracing tool exports segmentation training datasets.
authors:
  - given-names: Kinjalk
    family-names: Parth
    alias: MasterKinjalk
repository-code: "https://github.com/leakey-lab/Root-Mask-and-Skeletons"
url: "https://github.com/leakey-lab/Root-Mask-and-Skeletons"
keywords:
  - plant phenotyping
  - minirhizotron
  - root segmentation
  - skeletonization
  - root length
  - root area
  - deep learning
  - ground truth annotation
version: "3.0.0"
